      "sc:author": "URGI",
      "sc:description": "FAIDARE (FAIR Data-finder for Agronomic Research) was developed to meet the needs of the ELIXIR Plant Sciences community (https://elixir-europe.org/communities/plant-sciences).\nThe goal of this portal is to facilitate the discovery of public data on plant biology from an international federation of established data repositories. It is based on the “Breeding API” (BrAPI) specifications and facilitates access to genotyping and phenotyping datasets for crop and forest plants through an easy-to-use web interface. It also provides a standard interface that can be accessed programmatically via web services.\nIt is an extension of the generic DataDiscovery portal, a web portal that aims to provide researchers with quick and easy access to relevant biological data using specific keywords and filters. FAIDARE offers more detailed search and data extraction capabilities and capitalizes on the growing adoption of BrAPI.",
